    ('4e158e46-2cf3-422f-b0da-6868bedb431e'::uuid, 'card_description', 'For banded flint, people dug mainly with hatchets at Krzemionki, one of the largest known complexes of prehistoric flint mines in Europe, its mining area 4.5 km long.', 'One of Europe''s largest prehistoric flint mines, active from 3900-1600 BC. Underground shafts cut through Jurassic limestone in a complex rivaling Grime''s Graves.', 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:4e158e46-2cf3-422f-b0da-6868bedb431e:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description "One of Europe''s largest prehistoric flint mines, active from 3900-1600 BC. Underground shafts cut through Jurassic limestone in a complex rivaling Grime''s Graves." restored on Krzemionki', '7b25057c6ae05445c9056a433ec6273ec19bd43f6c0ebc27af52e50e950a6bfd|458644de21f2da2afc1571b607b111c070e214b0973a0c1a7f40e141e00c5b3a|458644de21f2da2afc1571b607b111c070e214b0973a0c1a7f40e141e00c5b3a', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "For banded flint, people dug mainly with hatchets at Krzemionki, one of the largest known complexes of prehistoric flint mines in Europe, its mining area 4.5 km long."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the mines at Krzemionki were for banded flint [S1]; people excavated the flint mainly with hatchets [S4]; Krzemionki is one of the largest known complexes of prehistoric flint mines in Europe [S2]; its mining area is 4.5 km long [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-028 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Krzemionki is a complex of prehistoric flint mines in Poland [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krzemionki]; The flint mined at Krzemionki is banded flint [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krzemionki]; People dug the flint at Krzemionki mainly with hatchets [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krzemionki]; Krzemionki is one of the largest known complexes of prehistoric flint mines in Europe [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krzemionki]; The mining area is 4.5 km long [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krzemionki]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4e7592eb-facc-4d84-a019-0d2f2311c1d0'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Rising 1,145 meters above sea level in the Sahyadri range, Jivdhan Fort was looted by the British between 1815 and 1818, yet its Main Gate and Kalyan gate remain in good condition.', '2nd-century BC hill fortress at 1,145 metres in the Sahyadri range. Jivdhan is one of the Famous 5 high-difficulty treks in Maharashtra, its sheer cliffs forming natural ramparts on all sides.', 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:4e7592eb-facc-4d84-a019-0d2f2311c1d0:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description ''2nd-century BC hill fortress at 1,145 metres in the Sahyadri range. Jivdhan is one of the Famous 5 high-difficulty treks in Maharashtra, its sheer cliffs forming natural ramparts on all sides.'' restored on Jivdhan Fort', 'e1aa18eaf365c00d52f5a493544c7d44e75da63b050660769888718b4330e20d|020012598faabdc1958f70eaaa747397573efab6ebc49c2579a38fb1bf3d23e8|020012598faabdc1958f70eaaa747397573efab6ebc49c2579a38fb1bf3d23e8', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Rising 1,145 meters above sea level in the Sahyadri range, Jivdhan Fort was looted by the British between 1815 and 1818, yet its Main Gate and Kalyan gate remain in good condition."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Jivdhan Fort rises 1,145 meters above sea level [S2]; it is in the Sahyadri mountain range [S2]; it was looted by the British between 1815 and 1818 [S3]; its Main Gate and Kalyan gate are in good condition [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-028 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Jivdhan Fort is a hill fortress in India (Maharashtra) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jivdhan]; The fort rises 1,145 meters above sea level [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jivdhan]; The fort is in the Sahyadri range [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jivdhan]; The fort was looted by the British between 1815 and 1818 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jivdhan]; The Main Gate and Kalyan gate of the fort remain in good condition [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jivdhan]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4f366f34-983c-42e1-a89d-7e8f5f77cdce'::uuid, 'card_description', NULL, 'Studies of skeletal remains found at Machu Picchu show that most people who lived there were immigrants from diverse backgrounds.', 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:4f366f34-983c-42e1-a89d-7e8f5f77cdce:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description ''Studies of skeletal remains found at Machu Picchu show that most people who lived there were immigrants from diverse backgrounds.'' restored on Machu Picchu', '||c2398fffdc17f4935396e3f988a8ff2a1080c6cf69340a8dd57859365762daa3', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: unproven-after-verify", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The web check could not prove: Machu Picchu stands at 2,430 meters; The web check could not prove: Machu Picchu lies on a mountain ridge; The web check could not prove: Machu Picchu is an Inca citadel"}]'::jsonb),
    ('505bd44a-9fec-4324-a414-4ee080bf37fa'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Clay works north of Katerini uncovered two Macedonian Tombs. In the western one, a double-winged marble door, completely preserved, separates the pre-chamber from the burial chamber.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:505bd44a-9fec-4324-a414-4ee080bf37fa:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description None restored on Macedonian Tombs, Katerini', '3648b0d5dbfab18658502592517a852dc5781135eeb9033c42d0ad6a165d1041|34e5b20b7a02dc8840211de21efd108018e667567afc27e010879b2fb5330adf|34e5b20b7a02dc8840211de21efd108018e667567afc27e010879b2fb5330adf', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Clay works north of Katerini uncovered two Macedonian Tombs. In the western one, a double-winged marble door, completely preserved, separates the pre-chamber from the burial chamber."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "works to recover clay uncovered the tombs [S1]; the site lies north of Katerini [S1]; two Macedonian tombs were discovered [S1]; the western tomb has a pre-chamber and a burial chamber [S3]; a double-winged marble door separates the two chambers [S4]; the marble door is completely preserved [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-029 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The site is a group of Macedonian tombs (burial monuments) located north of Katerini, Greece [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]; There are two such tombs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]; The two tombs were uncovered during clay works [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]; The western tomb has a pre-chamber and a burial chamber [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]; In the western tomb a door separates the pre-chamber from the burial chamber [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]; The door is double-winged and made of marble [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]; The marble door is completely preserved [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_Tombs,_Katerini]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('50a67cd0-367e-4f97-ac04-4e4cbbd7b1e6'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On two hilltops south of Tiaret stand the Jedars, thirteen Berber mausoleums built for royalty, as their size and commanding situation indicate, now in ruin after centuries of plunder.', 'Thirteen pre-Islamic Berber royal mausoleums from Late Antiquity, built on hilltops and plundered for centuries. Their builders remain a mystery.', 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:50a67cd0-367e-4f97-ac04-4e4cbbd7b1e6:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description ''Thirteen pre-Islamic Berber royal mausoleums from Late Antiquity, built on hilltops and plundered for centuries. Their builders remain a mystery.'' restored on Jedars', '76a13b34d92e01489a1bf923267738c84db1e98b6041c1f561e8fa3f1563b6b6|195ab602fd6d08a7515cdf016c849369d3143a8ab128731a689582c63ad3f3c3|195ab602fd6d08a7515cdf016c849369d3143a8ab128731a689582c63ad3f3c3', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On two hilltops south of Tiaret stand the Jedars, thirteen Berber mausoleums built for royalty, as their size and commanding situation indicate, now in ruin after centuries of plunder."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Jedars stand on two hilltops [S3]; they are south of Tiaret [S1, S3]; there are thirteen of them [S1]; they are Berber mausoleums [S1]; their size and commanding situation indicate they were built for royalty (kept as an indication) [S5]; they are in ruin after centuries of plunder [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-029 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The site is a group of Berber mausoleums (tombs) south of Tiaret, Algeria [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; There are thirteen of them [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; They are Berber mausoleums [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; They stand on two hilltops [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; They are located south of Tiaret [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; They were built for royalty, as their size and commanding situation indicate [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; They are now in ruin [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]; The ruin follows centuries of plunder [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedars]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('50cbcf03-2e37-4f82-9705-a55c9264b3d5'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Radiocarbon dates on human bone suggest use of the Tholos de Montelirio began in 2875–2700 BC. The site is closed to the public, but its objects wait in the Archeological Museum of Seville.', '3000–2800 BC megalithic tholos tomb in Seville Province — found in 1868 but unexcavated for decades. Resumed in 1980 due to urban sprawl, Montelirio remains closed; objects now in Seville museum.', 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:50cbcf03-2e37-4f82-9705-a55c9264b3d5:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description ''3000–2800 BC megalithic tholos tomb in Seville Province — found in 1868 but unexcavated for decades. Resumed in 1980 due to urban sprawl, Montelirio remains closed; objects now in Seville museum.'' restored on Tholos de Montelirio', 'f4f24c318d03553a4538b8b5162b71777d383248a59bbe1a5bf895ac957ca702|10054478ceecb59595a48fcc2a6bdc2cb86d4e9cd93bdd7288f2d03551d6adbc|10054478ceecb59595a48fcc2a6bdc2cb86d4e9cd93bdd7288f2d03551d6adbc', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Radiocarbon dates on human bone suggest use of the Tholos de Montelirio began in 2875–2700 BC. The site is closed to the public, but its objects wait in the Archeological Museum of Seville."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "radiocarbon dates on human bone suggest the dating (hedged) [S3]; use of the Tholos de Montelirio began in 2875–2700 BC [S3]; the site is closed to the public [S2]; its objects can be seen in the Archeological Museum of Seville [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-029 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Tholos de Montelirio is an archaeological site (a megalithic tholos construction) in Spain [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tholos_de_Montelirio]; The dating rests on radiocarbon dates on human bone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tholos_de_Montelirio]; Use of the tholos began in 2875-2700 BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tholos_de_Montelirio]; The site is closed to the public [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tholos_de_Montelirio]; Its objects are held in the Archeological Museum of Seville [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tholos_de_Montelirio]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('50f9ccc8-06b1-4283-af88-a6769d0b9083'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At the bottom of a narrow valley in Dorset stand the Nine Stones, a stone circle also called the Devil''s Nine Stones, where the roots of a beech tree have engulfed two of the megaliths.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:50f9ccc8-06b1-4283-af88-a6769d0b9083:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description None restored on Nine Stones, Winterbourne Abbas', '102d85a5dc3ca4f30eefb95cf8eef8530cae542da95a34f2a492f85cb2b3d698|30c8871180fa542491a18e3ca765487a6e7e7aaf554b66444f874fc447855970|30c8871180fa542491a18e3ca765487a6e7e7aaf554b66444f874fc447855970', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At the bottom of a narrow valley in Dorset stand the Nine Stones, a stone circle also called the Devil''s Nine Stones, where the roots of a beech tree have engulfed two of the megaliths."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Nine Stones stand at the bottom of a narrow valley [S6]; they are in Dorset [S1]; the Nine Stones is a stone circle [S1]; it is also called the Devil''s Nine Stones [S1]; the roots of a beech tree have engulfed two of the megaliths [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-029 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Nine Stones is a stone circle near Winterbourne Abbas in Dorset [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine_Stones,_Winterbourne_Abbas]; The site is in Dorset [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine_Stones,_Winterbourne_Abbas]; The circle is also called the Devil''s Nine Stones [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine_Stones,_W