    ('51db73ea-a48b-40dc-9d9e-f0f9b3a27cf6'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The Romans called it Aduatuca Tungrorum: Tongeren, the oldest town in Belgium and capital of a large Roman province, which may have been destroyed by the Huns in 451 AD.', 'Already in the fourth century, just as the Salian Franks were settling to the north, the city became the center of a Christian diocese under the influence of Saint Servatius, bishop of Tongeren.', 'teaser-card-s023-rollback:51db73ea-a48b-40dc-9d9e-f0f9b3a27cf6:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s023: card_description ''Already in the fourth century, just as the Salian Franks were settling to the north, the city became the center of a Christian diocese under the influence of Saint Servatius, bishop of Tongeren.'' restored on Tongeren', '1ff030b9d62d440e1318e92c60a0ad7aba3d0cc0561cf2405a52fb341a0839cd|fd27782aa675cb1c9ec16e78bdc709719426fe48e25c7296a56500b3178fe2de|fd27782aa675cb1c9ec16e78bdc709719426fe48e25c7296a56500b3178fe2de', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-010", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Romans called it Aduatuca Tungrorum: Tongeren, the oldest town in Belgium and capital of a large Roman province, which may have been destroyed by the Huns in 451 AD."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-010 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Romans called Tongeren Aduatuca Tungrorum [S2]; Tongeren is the oldest town in Belgium [S1]; it was the capital of a large Roman province [S2]; it may have been destroyed by the Huns in 451 AD (hedged) [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-029 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Tongeren is a town (city) in Belgium [SUPPORTED: h